window.POC_BANK=[{"id":"poc-001","concept":"Assessment","stem":"A new client reports chest pressure when climbing stairs but has never discussed it with a physician. What is the dental hygienist's BEST next step before beginning elective care?","choices":["Proceed but shorten the appointment","Complete treatment and document the symptom afterward","Clarify the symptom, assess urgency, and obtain appropriate medical consultation before elective care","Ask the client to sign a waiver"],"answer":2,"why":"Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。","pearl":"New symptoms that may affect safety belong in assessment before treatment, not in documentation after treatment.","rationales":[{"en":"“Proceed but shorten the appointment” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"“Proceed but shorten the appointment”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。"},{"en":"“Complete treatment and document the symptom afterward” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"“Complete treatment and document the symptom afterward”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Ask the client to sign a waiver” is not the best response. A signature cannot replace assessment, disclosure, understanding, or valid consent. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"“Ask the client to sign a waiver”不是最佳处理。签字不能取代评估、信息披露、理解和有效同意。 正确处理原则是：不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。"}]},{"id":"poc-002","concept":"Assessment","stem":"Which item is part of the subjective assessment?","choices":["Blood pressure reading","Client's description of sensitivity when drinking cold water","Probing depth of 6 mm","Radiographic bone loss"],"answer":1,"why":"Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。","pearl":"Subjective = reported. Objective = observed or measured.","rationales":[{"en":"“Blood pressure reading” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"“Blood pressure reading”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Probing depth of 6 mm” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"“Probing depth of 6 mm”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。"},{"en":"“Radiographic bone loss” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"“Radiographic bone loss”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。"}]},{"id":"poc-003","concept":"Assessment","stem":"A client states that their medical history has not changed. What should the dental hygienist do?","choices":["Accept the statement without review","Review and update the history at every appointment and document the response","Repeat the entire written questionnaire only once every five years","Ask only about medications"],"answer":1,"why":"Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。","pearl":"“No change” is still an assessment finding and should be documented.","rationales":[{"en":"“Accept the statement without review” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"“Accept the statement without review”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Repeat the entire written questionnaire only once every five years” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"“Repeat the entire written questionnaire only once every five years”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。"},{"en":"“Ask only about medications” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"“Ask only about medications”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。"}]},{"id":"poc-004","concept":"Vital Signs","stem":"A client's blood pressure is substantially higher than their usual readings. What is the BEST first action?","choices":["Ignore the value because the client feels well","Repeat the measurement after proper positioning and a short rest","Begin instrumentation immediately","Diagnose hypertension"],"answer":1,"why":"An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。","pearl":"Verify an abnormal vital sign before deciding what it means.","rationales":[{"en":"“Ignore the value because the client feels well” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"“Ignore the value because the client feels well”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Begin instrumentation immediately” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"“Begin instrumentation immediately”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。"},{"en":"“Diagnose hypertension” is not the best response. It exceeds the dental hygienist's role; the finding should be documented and appropriately referred. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"“Diagnose hypertension”不是最佳处理。这超出了牙科保健师的职责范围；应记录该发现并作适当转诊。 正确处理原则是：异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。"}]},{"id":"poc-005","concept":"Extraoral/Intraoral Examination","stem":"During an intraoral examination, a white lesion does not wipe off and has persisted for three weeks. What is the BEST action?","choices":["Record it as normal variation","Re-evaluate in one year","Document the lesion fully and arrange timely referral or further evaluation","Remove it with an explorer"],"answer":2,"why":"A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。","pearl":"Persistent, unexplained oral lesions should not be casually watched for long intervals.","rationales":[{"en":"“Record it as normal variation” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"“Record it as normal variation”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。"},{"en":"“Re-evaluate in one year” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"“Re-evaluate in one year”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Remove it with an explorer” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"“Remove it with an explorer”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。"}]},{"id":"poc-006","concept":"Periodontal Assessment","stem":"Which finding is most useful for detecting current gingival inflammation?","choices":["Bleeding on probing","Existing restoration","Tooth colour","Previous extraction"],"answer":0,"why":"Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。","pearl":"Bone loss shows past destruction; bleeding helps identify current inflammation.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Existing restoration” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"“Existing restoration”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。"},{"en":"“Tooth colour” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"“Tooth colour”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。"},{"en":"“Previous extraction” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"“Previous extraction”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。"}]},{"id":"poc-007","concept":"Periodontal Assessment","stem":"A 6-mm probing depth is recorded around a tooth. Which additional finding is essential for interpreting attachment loss?","choices":["Client's age only","Gingival margin position relative to the CEJ","Tooth shade","Salivary pH only"],"answer":1,"why":"Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。","pearl":"Pocket depth alone does not equal attachment loss.","rationales":[{"en":"“Client's age only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"“Client's age only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Tooth shade” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"“Tooth shade”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。"},{"en":"“Salivary pH only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"“Salivary pH only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。"}]},{"id":"poc-008","concept":"Risk Assessment","stem":"A client has well-controlled diabetes, smokes daily, and has generalized bleeding on probing. Which factor most strongly increases periodontal risk?","choices":["Daily smoking","Controlled diabetes alone","Client's eye colour","Use of an electric toothbrush"],"answer":0,"why":"Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。","pearl":"Risk assessment considers both disease indicators and modifiers.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Controlled diabetes alone” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"“Controlled diabetes alone”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。"},{"en":"“Client's eye colour” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"“Client's eye colour”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。"},{"en":"“Use of an electric toothbrush” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"“Use of an electric toothbrush”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。"}]},{"id":"poc-009","concept":"Dental Hygiene Diagnosis","stem":"Which statement is written most like a dental hygiene diagnosis?","choices":["Chronic periodontitis","Ineffective plaque control related to limited interdental cleaning, evidenced by generalized interproximal biofilm and bleeding","Prescribe antibiotics","The client needs a filling"],"answer":1,"why":"A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。","pearl":"Diagnosis connects the problem, contributing factors, and evidence.","rationales":[{"en":"“Chronic periodontitis” is not the best response. It represents a dental/medical diagnosis or treatment conclusion rather than a dental hygiene need statement. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"“Chronic periodontitis”不是最佳处理。这属于牙科或医学诊断/治疗结论，而不是牙科保健需要陈述。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Prescribe antibiotics” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"“Prescribe antibiotics”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。"},{"en":"“The client needs a filling” is not the best response. It represents a dental/medical diagnosis or treatment conclusion rather than a dental hygiene need statement. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"“The client needs a filling”不是最佳处理。这属于牙科或医学诊断/治疗结论，而不是牙科保健需要陈述。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。"}]},{"id":"poc-010","concept":"Dental Hygiene Diagnosis","stem":"What is the primary purpose of the dental hygiene diagnosis?","choices":["To replace the dentist's diagnosis","To identify client needs that guide dental hygiene interventions","To create a billing code only","To list every medical condition"],"answer":1,"why":"The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。","pearl":"Assessment gathers data; diagnosis gives the data clinical meaning.","rationales":[{"en":"“To replace the dentist's diagnosis” is not the best response. It represents a dental/medical diagnosis or treatment conclusion rather than a dental hygiene need statement. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"“To replace the dentist's diagnosis”不是最佳处理。这属于牙科或医学诊断/治疗结论，而不是牙科保健需要陈述。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“To create a billing code only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"“To create a billing code only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。"},{"en":"“To list every medical condition” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"“To list every medical condition”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。"}]},{"id":"poc-011","concept":"Planning","stem":"Which goal is most client-centred and measurable?","choices":["Client will improve oral hygiene","Client will reduce bleeding sites from 60% to 25% within eight weeks","Hygienist will explain flossing","Client should try harder"],"answer":1,"why":"A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。","pearl":"A measurable goal states what will change, by how much, and by when.","rationales":[{"en":"“Client will improve oral hygiene” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"“Client will improve oral hygiene”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Hygienist will explain flossing” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"“Hygienist will explain flossing”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。"},{"en":"“Client should try harder” is not the best response. It labels or pressures the client instead of identifying barriers and supporting achievable change. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"“Client should try harder”不是最佳处理。该做法给患者贴标签或施压，而不是识别障碍并支持可实现的改变。 正确处理原则是：优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。"}]},{"id":"poc-012","concept":"Planning","stem":"A client has acute oral pain, heavy calculus, and limited knowledge of home care. Which concern should generally be addressed first?","choices":["Long-term esthetic polishing","The acute problem affecting comfort and safety","A six-month recare date","Whitening options"],"answer":1,"why":"Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。","pearl":"Prioritize urgent, unstable, and safety-related needs first.","rationales":[{"en":"“Long-term esthetic polishing” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"“Long-term esthetic polishing”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“A six-month recare date” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"“A six-month recare date”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。"},{"en":"“Whitening options” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"“Whitening options”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。"}]},{"id":"poc-013","concept":"Planning","stem":"What should happen before a care plan is finalized?","choices":["The client should participate in reviewing options and goals","The hygienist should choose without discussion","All treatment must be completed","The record should be closed"],"answer":0,"why":"Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。","pearl":"A technically perfect plan can still fail if the client did not help shape it.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“The hygienist should choose without discussion” is not the best response. It excludes the client from decisions and is inconsistent with informed, shared decision-making. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"“The hygienist should choose without discussion”不是最佳处理。该做法排除了患者参与，不符合知情和共同决策原则。 正确处理原则是：共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。"},{"en":"“All treatment must be completed” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"“All treatment must be completed”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。"},{"en":"“The record should be closed” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"“The record should be closed”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。"}]},{"id":"poc-014","concept":"Informed Consent","stem":"Valid informed consent requires the client to understand:","choices":["Only the cost","The proposed care, material risks, benefits, alternatives, and consequences of declining","Only the clinician's preferred option","Every rare event ever reported"],"answer":1,"why":"Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。","pearl":"A signature is evidence of consent, not the whole consent process.","rationales":[{"en":"“Only the cost” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"“Only the cost”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Only the clinician's preferred option” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"“Only the clinician's preferred option”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。"},{"en":"“Every rare event ever reported” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"“Every rare event ever reported”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。"}]},{"id":"poc-015","concept":"Informed Consent","stem":"A capable client refuses recommended radiographs after the risks and alternatives are explained. What should the hygienist do?","choices":["Take them anyway","Respect the refusal, document the discussion, and determine whether safe care can still be provided","Dismiss the client immediately","Ask a family member to override the decision"],"answer":1,"why":"Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。","pearl":"Autonomy permits refusal; professional responsibility still limits unsafe care.","rationales":[{"en":"“Take them anyway” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"“Take them anyway”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Dismiss the client immediately” is not the best response. It is punitive rather than respectful, therapeutic, and clinically justified. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"“Dismiss the client immediately”不是最佳处理。该做法带有惩罚性，而非尊重、治疗性和有临床依据。 正确处理原则是：有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。"},{"en":"“Ask a family member to override the decision” is not the best response. A capable client's decision cannot be overridden by another person. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"“Ask a family member to override the decision”不是最佳处理。有决策能力患者的决定不能由他人推翻。 正确处理原则是：有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。"}]},{"id":"poc-016","concept":"Implementation","stem":"During instrumentation, the client develops wheezing and difficulty speaking. What should the hygienist do first?","choices":["Continue quickly","Stop treatment and begin emergency assessment and management","Finish polishing","Document it at the end"],"answer":1,"why":"A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。","pearl":"Implementation is never automatic; reassessment continues throughout care.","rationales":[{"en":"“Continue quickly” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"“Continue quickly”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Finish polishing” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"“Finish polishing”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。"},{"en":"“Document it at the end” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"“Document it at the end”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。"}]},{"id":"poc-017","concept":"Implementation","stem":"Which teaching strategy best supports client-centred implementation?","choices":["Give the same instructions to every client","Use plain language, demonstrate the skill, and ask the client to show it back","Provide a long lecture only","Avoid checking understanding"],"answer":1,"why":"Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。","pearl":"Teach-back tests the clarity of the teaching, not the intelligence of the client.","rationales":[{"en":"“Give the same instructions to every client” is not the best response. It does not adapt communication or verify the client's understanding and ability. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"“Give the same instructions to every client”不是最佳处理。该做法未调整沟通方式，也未确认患者的理解和操作能力。 正确处理原则是：使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Provide a long lecture only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"“Provide a long lecture only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"“Avoid checking understanding” is not the best response. It does not adapt communication or verify the client's understanding and ability. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"“Avoid checking understanding”不是最佳处理。该做法未调整沟通方式，也未确认患者的理解和操作能力。 正确处理原则是：使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。"}]},{"id":"poc-018","concept":"Implementation","stem":"A planned intervention becomes contraindicated because the client's health status changes. What is the BEST response?","choices":["Follow the original plan exactly","Modify or postpone care and document the reason","Delete the original assessment","Ask the client to decide whether it is safe"],"answer":1,"why":"The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。","pearl":"The care plan is a living clinical document, not a train locked to one track.","rationales":[{"en":"“Follow the original plan exactly” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"“Follow the original plan exactly”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Delete the original assessment” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"“Delete the original assessment”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。"},{"en":"“Ask the client to decide whether it is safe” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"“Ask the client to decide whether it is safe”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。"}]},{"id":"poc-019","concept":"Evaluation","stem":"At re-evaluation, bleeding on probing decreases from 70% to 30%, but the goal was below 20%. How should this be interpreted?","choices":["No improvement occurred","The goal was fully met","Meaningful improvement occurred, but the goal was only partially met","The original data should be discarded"],"answer":2,"why":"Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。","pearl":"Evaluation is not merely pass or fail; partial progress guides the next plan.","rationales":[{"en":"“No improvement occurred” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"“No improvement occurred”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。"},{"en":"“The goal was fully met” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"“The goal was fully met”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“The original data should be discarded” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"“The original data should be discarded”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。"}]},{"id":"poc-020","concept":"Evaluation","stem":"Which action best represents evaluation?","choices":["Collecting the original medical history","Comparing post-care outcomes with baseline findings and goals","Selecting instruments","Obtaining initial consent"],"answer":1,"why":"Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。","pearl":"Without a baseline and measurable goal, evaluation becomes guesswork.","rationales":[{"en":"“Collecting the original medical history” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"“Collecting the original medical history”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Selecting instruments” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"“Selecting instruments”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。"},{"en":"“Obtaining initial consent” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"“Obtaining initial consent”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。"}]},{"id":"poc-021","concept":"Documentation","stem":"Which entry is the most appropriate clinical documentation?","choices":["Client was difficult","Generalized bleeding noted; OHI reviewed with interdental brush demonstration; client successfully demonstrated technique","Everything normal","Good appointment"],"answer":1,"why":"Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。","pearl":"Document observable facts and professional actions, not labels or judgments.","rationales":[{"en":"“Client was difficult” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"“Client was difficult”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Everything normal” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"“Everything normal”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。"},{"en":"“Good appointment” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"“Good appointment”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。"}]},{"id":"poc-022","concept":"Documentation","stem":"An error is discovered in a completed clinical record. What is the BEST correction method?","choices":["Erase the original entry completely","Alter the date so the record looks correct","Make a transparent correction according to policy without obscuring the original entry","Delete the entire note"],"answer":2,"why":"Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。","pearl":"A corrected record should show what changed, when, and by whom.","rationales":[{"en":"“Erase the original entry completely” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"“Erase the original entry completely”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。"},{"en":"“Alter the date so the record looks correct” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"“Alter the date so the record looks correct”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Delete the entire note” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"“Delete the entire note”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。"}]},{"id":"poc-023","concept":"Documentation","stem":"Why should a client's refusal of recommended care be documented?","choices":["To punish the client","To record the information provided, the client's decision, and the plan for safe follow-up","Because refusal removes all clinician responsibility","Only for billing"],"answer":1,"why":"Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。","pearl":"Record the discussion and decision, not merely the word “refused.”","rationales":[{"en":"“To punish the client” is not the best response. It is punitive rather than respectful, therapeutic, and clinically justified. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"“To punish the client”不是最佳处理。该做法带有惩罚性，而非尊重、治疗性和有临床依据。 正确处理原则是：记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Because refusal removes all clinician responsibility” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"“Because refusal removes all clinician responsibility”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。"},{"en":"“Only for billing” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"“Only for billing”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。"}]},{"id":"poc-024","concept":"Sequencing","stem":"Which sequence best represents the dental hygiene process of care?","choices":["Implementation, assessment, evaluation, diagnosis, planning","Assessment, dental hygiene diagnosis, planning, implementation, evaluation","Planning, evaluation, assessment, implementation, diagnosis","Diagnosis, implementation, assessment, evaluation, planning"],"answer":1,"why":"The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。","pearl":"Documentation runs through every phase rather than appearing only at the end.","rationales":[{"en":"“Implementation, assessment, evaluation, diagnosis, planning” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"“Implementation, assessment, evaluation, diagnosis, planning”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Planning, evaluation, assessment, implementation, diagnosis” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"“Planning, evaluation, assessment, implementation, diagnosis”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。"},{"en":"“Diagnosis, implementation, assessment, evaluation, planning” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"“Diagnosis, implementation, assessment, evaluation, planning”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。"}]},{"id":"poc-025","concept":"Sequencing","stem":"A client returns after periodontal debridement. Before repeating the same intervention, the hygienist should first:","choices":["Reassess outcomes and current needs","Assume the original findings remain unchanged","Repeat treatment automatically","Schedule whitening"],"answer":0,"why":"Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。","pearl":"The next cycle begins with new assessment, not autopilot.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Assume the original findings remain unchanged” is not the best response. It relies on an unverified assumption instead of current assessment data. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"“Assume the original findings remain unchanged”不是最佳处理。该做法依赖未经核实的假设，而不是当前评估数据。 正确处理原则是：再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。"},{"en":"“Repeat treatment automatically” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"“Repeat treatment automatically”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。"},{"en":"“Schedule whitening” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"“Schedule whitening”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。"}]},{"id":"poc-026","concept":"Client-Centred Care","stem":"A client identifies reducing sensitivity as their main concern, while the hygienist is focused on plaque scores. What is the BEST approach?","choices":["Ignore the client's concern","Integrate the client's priority into assessment and planning while addressing clinical needs","Promise sensitivity will disappear","Treat only what the clinician prefers"],"answer":1,"why":"Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。","pearl":"The client's chief concern is clinically useful data, not a side note.","rationales":[{"en":"“Ignore the client's concern” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"“Ignore the client's concern”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Promise sensitivity will disappear” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"“Promise sensitivity will disappear”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。"},{"en":"“Treat only what the clinician prefers” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"“Treat only what the clinician prefers”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。"}]},{"id":"poc-027","concept":"Client-Centred Care","stem":"Which action best supports shared decision-making?","choices":["Present one option as the only acceptable choice","Discuss reasonable options and invite the client to weigh them according to personal values","Use technical language to discourage questions","Ask for a signature before explaining care"],"answer":1,"why":"Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。","pearl":"Shared decisions require real options and a real voice.","rationales":[{"en":"“Present one option as the only acceptable choice” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"“Present one option as the only acceptable choice”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Use technical language to discourage questions” is not the best response. It does not adapt communication or verify the client's understanding and ability. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"“Use technical language to discourage questions”不是最佳处理。该做法未调整沟通方式，也未确认患者的理解和操作能力。 正确处理原则是：共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。"},{"en":"“Ask for a signature before explaining care” is not the best response. A signature cannot replace assessment, disclosure, understanding, or valid consent. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"“Ask for a signature before explaining care”不是最佳处理。签字不能取代评估、信息披露、理解和有效同意。 正确处理原则是：共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。"}]},{"id":"poc-028","concept":"Referral and Collaboration","stem":"An assessment finding is outside the dental hygienist's scope to diagnose. What is the BEST action?","choices":["Ignore it","Provide a definitive diagnosis anyway","Document the finding and make an appropriate referral or consultation","Ask the client to search online"],"answer":2,"why":"The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。","pearl":"Recognizing a problem is not the same as claiming authority to diagnose it.","rationales":[{"en":"“Ignore it” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"“Ignore it”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。"},{"en":"“Provide a definitive diagnosis anyway” is not the best response. It exceeds the dental hygienist's role; the finding should be documented and appropriately referred. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"“Provide a definitive diagnosis anyway”不是最佳处理。这超出了牙科保健师的职责范围；应记录该发现并作适当转诊。 正确处理原则是：当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Ask the client to search online” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"“Ask the client to search online”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。"}]},{"id":"poc-029","concept":"Quality Improvement","stem":"A clinic notices that many clients miss recommended re-evaluation appointments. Which response best reflects quality improvement?","choices":["Blame the clients","Review the process, identify barriers, test a reminder strategy, and measure whether attendance improves","Stop scheduling re-evaluations","Change the records"],"answer":1,"why":"Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。","pearl":"Quality improvement studies the process, not just the person.","rationales":[{"en":"“Blame the clients” is not the best response. It is punitive rather than respectful, therapeutic, and clinically justified. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"“Blame the clients”不是最佳处理。该做法带有惩罚性，而非尊重、治疗性和有临床依据。 正确处理原则是：质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Stop scheduling re-evaluations” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"“Stop scheduling re-evaluations”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。"},{"en":"“Change the records” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"“Change the records”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。"}]},{"id":"poc-030","concept":"Comprehensive Case","stem":"A client with generalized inflammation has not used interdental aids and says, “I do not think I can manage floss.” Which plan is BEST?","choices":["Document noncompliance and end the discussion","Select an easier interdental aid, demonstrate it, use teach-back, and set a measurable short-term goal","Insist on floss only","Delay all education until disease resolves"],"answer":1,"why":"The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。","pearl":"Adapt the method without abandoning the clinical objective.","rationales":[{"en":"“Document noncompliance and end the discussion” is not the best response. It labels or pressures the client instead of identifying barriers and supporting achievable change. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"“Document noncompliance and end the discussion”不是最佳处理。该做法给患者贴标签或施压，而不是识别障碍并支持可实现的改变。 正确处理原则是：该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Insist on floss only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"“Insist on floss only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"“Delay all education until disease resolves” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"“Delay all education until disease resolves”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。"}]},{"id":"poc-031","concept":"Dental Hygiene Diagnosis","stem":"Assessment reveals generalized bleeding on probing, heavy interproximal biofilm, and no radiographic bone loss. Which dental hygiene diagnosis is MOST appropriate?","choices":["Periodontitis caused by irreversible attachment loss","Inflammation related to ineffective interproximal biofilm control","Dental caries caused only by sugar intake","A medical diagnosis of gingivitis"],"answer":1,"why":"A dental hygiene diagnosis describes the client response or unmet need that dental hygiene care can address. The findings support inflammation related to inadequate interproximal plaque control, without evidence of attachment loss.","zh":"牙科卫生诊断应描述可由牙科卫生护理改善的患者反应或未满足需要。该病例支持与邻面菌斑控制不足相关的炎症，且无附着丧失证据。","pearl":"Name the modifiable client problem, not a medical diagnosis.","rationales":[{"en":"Periodontitis is not supported because the case states there is no radiographic bone loss or attachment-loss evidence.","zh":"病例明确无影像学骨丧失或附着丧失证据，因此不能支持牙周炎。"},{"en":"This choice links the observed inflammation to a modifiable oral self-care factor that dental hygiene interventions can address.","zh":"该选项把观察到的炎症与可改善的口腔自我护理因素联系起来，符合牙科卫生干预范围。"},{"en":"The findings concern gingival inflammation and interproximal biofilm, not a caries diagnosis or a single dietary cause.","zh":"这些发现涉及牙龈炎症和邻面菌斑，而不是龋病诊断或单一饮食原因。"},{"en":"Dental hygienists formulate dental hygiene diagnoses; they should not present a medical diagnosis as their own.","zh":"牙科卫生师应制定牙科卫生诊断，而不是把医学诊断作为自己的诊断。"}]},{"id":"poc-032","concept":"Planning","stem":"Which care-plan goal is the MOST measurable and client-centred?","choices":["The client will improve oral hygiene soon","The clinician will remove all deposits","Within four weeks, the client will demonstrate daily interdental cleaning at three selected sites and bleeding will decrease from baseline","The client will understand periodontal disease"],"answer":2,"why":"A useful goal specifies who will do what, by when, and how success will be measured. It also reflects an outcome meaningful to the client.","zh":"有效目标应明确由谁、在何时完成什么，并说明如何衡量成功，同时体现对患者有意义的结果。","pearl":"A measurable goal has a behaviour, timeframe, and outcome indicator.","rationales":[{"en":"“Improve” and “soon” are vague and cannot be evaluated reliably.","zh":"“改善”和“很快”含糊，无法可靠评价。"},{"en":"This is a clinician task, not a client outcome or behavioural goal.","zh":"这是临床人员的任务，不是患者结果或行为目标。"},{"en":"This goal includes a specific behaviour, selected sites, a four-week timeframe, and a measurable bleeding outcome.","zh":"该目标包含具体行为、选定部位、四周时限和可测量的出血结果。"},{"en":"“Understand” is not operationally defined, so achievement cannot be confirmed.","zh":"“理解”未被操作性定义，因此无法确认是否达成。"}]},{"id":"poc-033","concept":"Sequencing","stem":"A client has uncontrolled pain from a suspected acute dental infection and also requires extensive preventive care. What should occur FIRST?","choices":["Complete all preventive education before addressing pain","Arrange urgent assessment or referral for the acute condition, then continue the comprehensive plan when safe","Begin elective debridement because it is on the care plan","Wait until the next recare visit"],"answer":1,"why":"Urgent conditions that threaten comfort or safety take priority. The comprehensive dental hygiene plan can continue after the acute problem is assessed and stabilized.","zh":"影响舒适或安全的急性问题应优先处理。急性问题评估并稳定后，再继续综合牙科卫生计划。","pearl":"Sequence care by urgency and safety before routine prevention.","rationales":[{"en":"Education remains important, but it should not delay assessment of an acute painful condition.","zh":"教育很重要，但不应延误急性疼痛问题的评估。"},{"en":"This sequence addresses the urgent problem first and preserves the longer-term preventive plan.","zh":"该顺序先处理紧急问题，同时保留长期预防计划。"},{"en":"Elective debridement should not precede evaluation of a potentially spreading acute infection.","zh":"在可能扩散的急性感染得到评估前，不应先进行选择性洁治。"},{"en":"Deferring an acute painful condition until recare could allow deterioration and is not appropriate triage.","zh":"把急性疼痛问题推迟到复诊可能导致恶化，不符合正确分诊。"}]},{"id":"poc-034","concept":"Implementation","stem":"During instrumentation, the client reports sharp pain and withdraws consent to continue. What is the BEST response?","choices":["Continue because consent was signed earlier","Stop, assess the cause, discuss options, and obtain renewed consent before proceeding","Ask an assistant to hold the client still","Document the refusal only after finishing"],"answer":1,"why":"Consent is ongoing and may be withdrawn at any time. The clinician must stop, assess, communicate, and obtain valid consent for any revised approach.","zh":"知情同意是持续过程，患者可随时撤回。临床人员必须停止操作、评估、沟通，并在调整方案前重新取得有效同意。","pearl":"A signed form never overrides present withdrawal of consent.","rationales":[{"en":"Earlier consent does not authorize treatment after the client clearly withdraws it.","zh":"患者明确撤回同意后，先前签署的同意不能继续授权治疗。"},{"en":"Stopping and reassessing respects autonomy and allows a safe, mutually agreed plan.","zh":"停止并重新评估可尊重自主权，并制定安全、双方同意的方案。"},{"en":"Restraining a competent client for elective care is coercive and unsafe.","zh":"为选择性治疗限制有能力患者的行动具有强迫性且不安全。"},{"en":"Finishing despite withdrawal violates consent; documentation does not cure that breach.","zh":"在撤回同意后仍完成治疗违反知情同意，事后记录不能弥补。"}]},{"id":"poc-035","concept":"Evaluation","stem":"At re-evaluation six weeks after nonsurgical periodontal therapy, bleeding has decreased substantially but several 6 mm sites still bleed and retain calculus. What is the BEST next step?","choices":["Declare treatment complete because overall bleeding improved","Reassess contributing factors, provide site-specific retreatment or referral as indicated, and revise the maintenance plan","Repeat the original plan without documenting findings","Schedule routine yearly care only"],"answer":1,"why":"Evaluation compares current findings with baseline and goals. Persistent deep bleeding sites require targeted reassessment and modification of care, not automatic discharge.","zh":"评价应将当前结果与基线和目标比较。持续存在的深袋出血部位需要针对性重新评估并调整护理，而不是自动结束治疗。","pearl":"Improvement does not erase unresolved high-risk sites.","rationales":[{"en":"Global improvement is encouraging, but persistent deep bleeding sites still require action.","zh":"总体改善值得肯定，但持续的深袋出血部位仍需处理。"},{"en":"This uses re-evaluation findings to individualize retreatment, referral, and maintenance.","zh":"该做法利用复评结果个体化安排再治疗、转诊和维护。"},{"en":"Repeating a plan without analyzing new findings ignores the purpose of evaluation.","zh":"不分析新发现而机械重复原计划，忽略了评价的目的。"},{"en":"Yearly care is unlikely to be appropriate for unresolved deep bleeding sites.","zh":"对于尚未解决的深袋出血部位，仅安排年度护理通常不合适。"}]},{"id":"poc-036","concept":"Documentation","stem":"Which entry BEST documents a client declining recommended radiographs?","choices":["Client difficult; refused x-rays","No x-rays today","Recommended bitewings, explained purpose, benefits and limitations of declining; client verbalized understanding and declined; dentist notified as applicable","Client signed waiver"],"answer":2,"why":"A defensible record is objective and records the recommendation, information provided, client understanding, decision, and relevant follow-up.","zh":"具有法律和临床价值的记录应客观记载建议、已提供的信息、患者理解、决定及相关后续措施。","pearl":"Document informed refusal, not a label or a bare signature.","rationales":[{"en":"Calling the client “difficult” is judgmental and omits the informed-refusal discussion.","zh":"称患者“难处理”带有评判性，也遗漏了知情拒绝讨论。"},{"en":"This entry states only the outcome and does not show what was recommended or explained.","zh":"该记录只说明结果，没有显示建议内容或解释过程。"},{"en":"This entry objectively captures recommendation, disclosure, understanding, refusal, and follow-up.","zh":"该记录客观涵盖建议、信息披露、理解、拒绝和后续措施。"},{"en":"A signature alone does not document the substance of informed refusal.","zh":"仅有签字不能记录知情拒绝的实质过程。"}]},{"id":"poc-037","concept":"Assessment","stem":"A client taking warfarin reports a recent dose change and frequent unexplained bruising. What is the BEST action before invasive instrumentation?","choices":["Tell the client to stop warfarin for three days","Ignore the bruising because warfarin use is common","Clarify the change, assess bleeding history, and obtain appropriate prescriber consultation or current laboratory information when indicated","Proceed and use more pressure afterward"],"answer":2,"why":"A medication change plus new bruising may alter bleeding risk. The hygienist should gather relevant information and collaborate rather than independently stopping medication.","zh":"药物剂量变化并出现新发瘀青可能改变出血风险。牙科卫生师应收集相关信息并适当会诊，而不能自行停药。","pearl":"Assess and collaborate; never independently discontinue prescribed anticoagulants.","rationales":[{"en":"Only the prescriber should direct interruption of anticoagulant therapy.","zh":"只有处方医师可以决定是否中断抗凝治疗。"},{"en":"New bruising after a dose change is clinically relevant and should not be dismissed.","zh":"剂量变化后的新发瘀青具有临床意义，不应忽视。"},{"en":"This response verifies risk and supports coordinated, safe decision-making.","zh":"该做法核实风险并支持协作、安全的决策。"},{"en":"Postoperative pressure does not replace pre-treatment risk assessment.","zh":"术后加压不能替代治疗前风险评估。"}]},{"id":"poc-038","concept":"Risk Assessment","stem":"Which finding has the GREATEST effect on a caries-risk plan for an adult with several new root-surface lesions?","choices":["Favourite toothpaste flavour","Daily xerostomia from medication and frequent sipping of sweetened drinks","Preference for morning appointments","One old amalgam restoration"],"answer":1,"why":"Reduced salivary protection combined with frequent fermentable-carbohydrate exposure strongly increases root-caries risk and should shape preventive interventions and recall.","zh":"唾液保护减少并频繁摄入可发酵碳水化合物，会显著增加根面龋风险，应影响预防干预和复诊安排。","pearl":"Risk assessment identifies active drivers that can change the care plan.","rationales":[{"en":"Flavour preference may affect product acceptance but is not the major biological risk driver here.","zh":"牙膏口味可能影响接受度，但不是此病例的主要生物学风险因素。"},{"en":"Xerostomia and frequent sugar exposure directly increase demineralization risk and reduce repair capacity.","zh":"口干和频繁糖暴露会直接增加脱矿风险并降低修复能力。"},{"en":"Appointment timing does not explain the new root-surface disease pattern.","zh":"就诊时间偏好不能解释新发根面龋模式。"},{"en":"A stable old restoration alone is not the strongest current risk indicator.","zh":"一处稳定的旧修复体本身不是最强的当前风险指标。"}]},{"id":"poc-039","concept":"Planning","stem":"A client is at high caries risk, has limited dexterity, and cannot tolerate a complicated home-care routine. Which plan is BEST?","choices":["Provide six new products at once","Select the highest-priority simple interventions, demonstrate them, and stage additional changes over time","Use the same plan given to every high-risk client","Delay prevention until restorative treatment is complete"],"answer":1,"why":"A realistic plan prioritizes evidence-based interventions and matches the client’s ability and readiness. Staging changes improves feasibility and adherence.","zh":"现实的计划应优先选择循证干预，并符合患者的能力和准备程度。分阶段改变可提高可行性和坚持度。","pearl":"The best plan is effective enough to matter and simple enough to use.","rationales":[{"en":"Too many simultaneous changes can overwhelm the client and reduce adherence.","zh":"同时提出过多改变可能使患者不堪重负并降低依从性。"},{"en":"This choice balances disease risk with dexterity, burden, and achievable behaviour change.","zh":"该选项在疾病风险、手部灵活性、负担和可实现行为改变之间取得平衡。"},{"en":"Standardized plans ignore individual barriers, preferences, and risk factors.","zh":"统一计划忽略个体障碍、偏好和风险因素。"},{"en":"Preventive measures should begin promptly and complement restorative care.","zh":"预防措施应及时开始，并与修复治疗相配合。"}]},{"id":"poc-040","concept":"Referral and Collaboration","stem":"A client has a persistent ulcer with indurated borders for more than two weeks. The dentist is unavailable that day. What is the dental hygienist’s BEST action?","choices":["Wait until the next six-month visit","Document complete lesion characteristics and arrange timely referral according to clinic protocol","Tell the client it is cancer","Apply topical anesthetic and close the record"],"answer":1,"why":"A persistent indurated ulcer requires prompt further evaluation. The hygienist should document objective findings and facilitate referral without making a definitive diagnosis.","zh":"持续超过两周且边缘硬结的溃疡需要及时进一步评估。牙科卫生师应客观记录并促成转诊，而不能作出确诊。","pearl":"Urgent referral can be appropriate even when definitive diagnosis is outside scope.","rationales":[{"en":"A six-month delay is unsafe for a potentially serious persistent lesion.","zh":"对可能严重的持续性病变延迟六个月是不安全的。"},{"en":"This response supports timely evaluation while staying within scope.","zh":"该做法既促成及时评估，又符合执业范围。"},{"en":"The finding is suspicious, but the hygienist should not declare a cancer diagnosis.","zh":"该发现可疑，但牙科卫生师不应直接宣布癌症诊断。"},{"en":"Symptom relief alone does not address the need for diagnosis and follow-up.","zh":"仅缓解症状不能满足诊断和随访需要。"}]},{"id":"poc-041","concept":"Evaluation","stem":"A client’s plaque score is unchanged at re-evaluation despite receiving detailed verbal instructions. What is the BEST response?","choices":["Repeat the same lecture more forcefully","Explore barriers, observe the client’s technique, adapt the method, and use teach-back","Document that the client is unmotivated","Discontinue preventive care"],"answer":1,"why":"Evaluation should identify why the goal was not met and guide a revised intervention. Direct observation and teach-back reveal skill or feasibility barriers.","zh":"评价应找出目标未达成的原因并指导调整干预。直接观察和回示教学可发现技能或可行性障碍。","pearl":"When outcomes stall, change the strategy before blaming the client.","rationales":[{"en":"More intensity does not correct a mismatched or poorly understood method.","zh":"仅增加训导力度不能纠正不匹配或未理解的方法。"},{"en":"This approach reassesses barriers and verifies actual skill before revising the plan.","zh":"该方法重新评估障碍并确认实际技能，然后调整计划。"},{"en":"“Unmotivated” is a judgmental label and does not explain the observed outcome.","zh":"“缺乏动力”是评判性标签，不能解释观察到的结果。"},{"en":"Stopping prevention abandons an unmet need rather than modifying care.","zh":"停止预防护理是在放弃未满足需要，而不是调整护理。"}]},{"id":"poc-042","concept":"Comprehensive Case","stem":"A client with diabetes has generalized bleeding, a dry mouth, irregular meals, and difficulty affording recommended products. Which plan is MOST client-centred?","choices":["Focus only on calculus removal","Prioritize inflammation control and xerostomia management, coordinate medical concerns when needed, and choose affordable strategies with the client","Recommend the most expensive products because they are best","Delay care until the client’s finances improve"],"answer":1,"why":"Comprehensive planning integrates systemic factors, oral findings, social barriers, and client preferences. Affordable, prioritized interventions are more likely to be used.","zh":"综合计划应整合全身因素、口腔发现、社会障碍和患者偏好。可负担且有优先顺序的干预更可能被采用。","pearl":"Clinical excellence includes feasibility and access, not just ideal products.","rationales":[{"en":"Calculus removal alone ignores xerostomia, diabetes-related risk, behaviour, and access barriers.","zh":"仅去除牙石忽略了口干、糖尿病相关风险、行为和经济障碍。"},{"en":"This choice integrates the client’s oral, medical, and financial context into achievable care.","zh":"该选项把患者的口腔、医学和经济背景整合为可实现的护理。"},{"en":"Costly products are not automatically superior and may be unusable for this client.","zh":"昂贵产品并非自动更优，且患者可能无法使用。"},{"en":"Financial barriers call for adaptation and support, not indefinite postponement.","zh":"经济障碍需要调整和支持，而不是无限期推迟。"}]},{"id":"poc-043","concept":"Informed Consent","stem":"A client with limited English nods during the explanation of periodontal therapy but cannot describe the proposed treatment. What is the BEST action?","choices":["Assume nodding means consent","Use qualified interpretation or another appropriate communication aid, explain again, and verify understanding with teach-back","Ask a family child to translate complex risks","Proceed because the treatment is beneficial"],"answer":1,"why":"Valid consent requires understanding. Communication must be adapted, and teach-back should confirm comprehension before treatment.","zh":"有效同意要求患者真正理解。应调整沟通方式，并在治疗前通过回示确认理解。","pearl":"Agreement without demonstrated understanding is not informed consent.","rationales":[{"en":"Nodding may reflect politeness or confusion and does not prove understanding.","zh":"点头可能出于礼貌或困惑，不能证明理解。"},{"en":"Qualified communication support and teach-back protect accuracy, autonomy, and consent validity.","zh":"合格的沟通支持和回示教学可保障准确性、自主权和同意有效性。"},{"en":"A child may not accurately translate complex clinical risks and may compromise privacy.","zh":"儿童可能无法准确翻译复杂临床风险，也可能影响隐私。"},{"en":"Beneficence does not permit treatment without valid informed consent.","zh":"有益原则不能取代有效的知情同意。"}]},{"id":"poc-044","concept":"Documentation","stem":"After signing a chart entry, the dental hygienist notices an incorrect tooth number. What is the BEST correction?","choices":["Delete the original entry completely","Alter the number without indicating a change","Make a dated correction or addendum according to policy while preserving the original record","Ask another staff member to rewrite the note"],"answer":2,"why":"Records must remain accurate and transparent. Corrections should preserve the original information and clearly identify the amendment, date, and author.","zh":"病历必须准确且透明。更正应保留原始信息，并清楚标明修改内容、日期和作者。","pearl":"Correct the record without making its history disappear.","rationales":[{"en":"Deleting the original can destroy the audit trail and compromise record integrity.","zh":"删除原始记录会破坏审计轨迹并影响病历完整性。"},{"en":"An invisible alteration makes the record misleading and unauditable.","zh":"无痕修改会使病历具有误导性且无法审计。"},{"en":"A transparent correction preserves both accuracy and the record’s chronology.","zh":"透明更正同时保留准确性和病历时间顺序。"},{"en":"The clinician responsible for the entry should make the correction according to policy.","zh":"应由负责该记录的临床人员按照规定进行更正。"}]},{"id":"poc-045","concept":"Implementation","stem":"During ultrasonic instrumentation, aerosol control is inadequate because the high-volume evacuation system stops working. What is the BEST action?","choices":["Continue at full power","Pause and modify or postpone the procedure until safe controls are restored","Ask the client to hold their breath","Document the equipment failure after completing treatment"],"answer":1,"why":"Implementation must follow infection-prevention and safety requirements. When essential controls fail, treatment should be modified or stopped until risk is adequately managed.","zh":"实施护理必须遵循感染预防和安全要求。当关键控制措施失效时，应调整或停止治疗，直到风险得到充分控制。","pearl":"A planned procedure never outranks immediate safety controls.","rationales":[{"en":"Continuing creates avoidable exposure and ignores the failed control.","zh":"继续操作会造成可避免的暴露，并忽视控制措施失效。"},{"en":"Pausing allows the clinician to restore controls or select a safer alternative.","zh":"暂停可使临床人员恢复控制措施或选择更安全的替代方法。"},{"en":"Breath-holding is neither realistic nor an adequate aerosol-control measure.","zh":"让患者屏住呼吸既不现实，也不是充分的气溶胶控制措施。"},{"en":"Documentation is necessary but does not justify unsafe continuation.","zh":"记录是必要的，但不能成为不安全继续操作的理由。"}]},{"id":"poc-046","concept":"Planning","stem":"Which factor should MOST influence the interval for periodontal maintenance?","choices":["The clinic’s usual six-month schedule","The client’s current disease stability, risk factors, self-care, and response to therapy","The client’s age alone","Insurance frequency limits"],"answer":1,"why":"Maintenance intervals should be individualized from current risk and treatment response, rather than assigned automatically by calendar or coverage.","zh":"牙周维护间隔应根据当前风险和治疗反应个体化，而不是仅按日历或保险规定自动安排。","pearl":"Recall is a clinical decision, not a default date.","rationales":[{"en":"A routine schedule may be too long or too short for the individual client.","zh":"固定常规间隔对个体患者可能过长或过短。"},{"en":"These factors directly reflect recurrence risk and the need for professional support.","zh":"这些因素直接反映复发风险和专业支持需要。"},{"en":"Age alone cannot represent disease activity, behaviour, or systemic risk.","zh":"年龄本身不能代表疾病活动、行为或全身风险。"},{"en":"Coverage may affect access but should not define the clinically recommended interval.","zh":"保险可能影响可及性，但不应决定临床建议间隔。"}]},{"id":"poc-047","concept":"Dental Hygiene Diagnosis","stem":"A client avoids smiling because of visible anterior staining and says this affects social confidence. Which unmet human need is MOST directly reflected?","choices":["Freedom from head and neck pain","Wholesome facial image","Protection from health risks","Biologically sound dentition"],"answer":1,"why":"Concern about appearance and social confidence most directly reflects the need for a wholesome facial image.","zh":"对外观和社交自信的担忧最直接反映“健康面容形象”的需要。","pearl":"Choose the need most directly expressed by the client’s words.","rationales":[{"en":"No pain complaint is described in the scenario.","zh":"情境中没有描述疼痛主诉。"},{"en":"The client specifically links visible staining with appearance and confidence.","zh":"患者明确把可见染色与外观和自信联系起来。"},{"en":"Although prevention matters, the stated concern is appearance rather than an unrecognized health hazard.","zh":"尽管预防很重要，但患者表达的是外观问题，而不是未识别的健康风险。"},{"en":"The teeth may be biologically sound; the expressed unmet need concerns facial image.","zh":"牙齿可能在生物学上健康，患者表达的未满足需要是面容形象。"}]},{"id":"poc-048","concept":"Evidence-Based Care","stem":"A new product advertisement claims it “eliminates periodontal disease.” What is the BEST approach before recommending it?","choices":["Rely on the advertisement because it is recent","Search for relevant high-quality evidence, appraise its validity and applicability, and integrate it with clinical expertise and client preferences","Recommend it if a colleague likes it","Avoid all new products"],"answer":1,"why":"Evidence-based care integrates critically appraised research, clinical expertise, and the client’s circumstances and preferences.","zh":"循证护理整合经过批判性评价的研究证据、临床专业判断以及患者情况和偏好。","pearl":"Novelty and marketing are not evidence hierarchies.","rationales":[{"en":"Recency and advertising language do not establish validity or clinical benefit.","zh":"新颖性和广告措辞不能证明有效性或临床获益。"},{"en":"This is the complete evidence-based decision process.","zh":"这是完整的循证决策过程。"},{"en":"A colleague’s experience may generate a question but cannot replace appraisal of evidence.","zh":"同事经验可提示问题，但不能取代证据评价。"},{"en":"Automatically rejecting innovation is no more evidence-based than automatically accepting it.","zh":"一概拒绝创新并不比一概接受更符合循证原则。"}]},{"id":"poc-049","concept":"Evaluation","stem":"Which finding BEST demonstrates that a behavioural objective was achieved?","choices":["The dental hygienist explained flossing","The client says the appointment was helpful","The client correctly demonstrates the selected interdental aid at the target sites without prompting","A brochure was provided"],"answer":2,"why":"Achievement of a behavioural objective is demonstrated by observable client performance, not merely by delivery of education.","zh":"行为目标是否达成，应通过可观察的患者表现来证明，而不是仅凭提供了教育。","pearl":"Measure what the client can now do.","rationales":[{"en":"This documents the clinician’s action, not the client’s learning outcome.","zh":"这记录的是临床人员的行为，而不是患者的学习结果。"},{"en":"Satisfaction is valuable but does not demonstrate the specified skill.","zh":"满意度有价值，但不能证明具体技能。"},{"en":"Independent correct demonstration is direct evidence that the skill objective was met.","zh":"患者能独立正确示范，是技能目标达成的直接证据。"},{"en":"Providing material does not establish that it was understood or applied.","zh":"提供资料不能证明患者已理解或应用。"}]},{"id":"poc-050","concept":"Comprehensive Case","stem":"A client has 7 mm pockets, mobility, uncontrolled smoking, and has never received periodontal therapy. Which care sequence is BEST?","choices":["Provide cosmetic polishing first","Complete comprehensive assessment, discuss diagnosis and risk, obtain consent, initiate indicated nonsurgical therapy and risk-factor support, then re-evaluate and refer as needed","Schedule annual maintenance without active therapy","Refer immediately without explaining findings"],"answer":1,"why":"The process of care moves from comprehensive assessment and informed planning to implementation, re-evaluation, and appropriate collaboration. Smoking support and referral are integrated rather than isolated.","zh":"护理过程应从综合评估和知情计划开始，再实施治疗、复评并适当协作。戒烟支持和转诊应整合其中。","pearl":"Complex disease still follows the clinical cycle, with urgency and collaboration woven in.","rationales":[{"en":"Cosmetic polishing does not address the active periodontal disease and risk factors.","zh":"美容抛光不能处理活动性牙周病和风险因素。"},{"en":"This sequence integrates assessment, consent, active care, risk modification, evaluation, and referral.","zh":"该顺序整合评估、同意、积极治疗、风险改变、评价和转诊。"},{"en":"Maintenance alone is not adequate before active disease has been assessed and treated.","zh":"在活动性疾病得到评估和治疗前，仅做维护是不充分的。"},{"en":"Referral may be appropriate, but the client should still receive explanation, documentation, and coordinated care.","zh":"转诊可能适当，但仍应向患者解释、记录并协调护理。"}]},{"id":"poc-051","concept":"Assessment","stem":"During medication reconciliation, the client reports taking an herbal supplement but does not know the name. What is the BEST response?","choices":["Record “herbal product” and proceed","Ask the client to identify or bring the product, clarify dose and purpose, and evaluate possible treatment implications","Tell the client all supplements are harmless","Remove it from the history because it is not a prescription"],"answer":1,"why":"Nonprescription and herbal products can affect bleeding, sedation, blood pressure, and drug interactions. Accurate identification is part of a complete medication history.","zh":"非处方药和草药产品可能影响出血、镇静、血压及药物相互作用。准确识别是完整用药史的一部分。","pearl":"Medication reconciliation includes everything the client takes.","rationales":[{"en":"A vague entry does not provide enough information to assess safety.","zh":"含糊记录不足以评估安全性。"},{"en":"This obtains the details needed to evaluate interactions and care modifications.","zh":"该做法获取评估相互作用和护理调整所需的详细信息。"},{"en":"Some supplements have clinically important effects and interactions.","zh":"某些补充剂具有重要临床作用和相互作用。"},{"en":"Nonprescription status does not make a product irrelevant to treatment.","zh":"非处方身份并不意味着该产品与治疗无关。"}]},{"id":"poc-052","concept":"Client-Centred Care","stem":"A client repeatedly misses morning appointments because of night-shift work. What is the BEST care-planning response?","choices":["Label the client noncompliant","Explore scheduling barriers and offer feasible appointment times while maintaining needed care intervals","Discharge the client immediately","Keep booking mornings to teach responsibility"],"answer":1,"why":"Client-centred planning identifies practical barriers and adapts delivery without abandoning clinical goals.","zh":"以患者为中心的计划应识别实际障碍并调整服务方式，同时不放弃临床目标。","pearl":"Adapt the pathway, not the standard of care.","rationales":[{"en":"A label does not solve the scheduling barrier and can damage the therapeutic relationship.","zh":"贴标签不能解决排班障碍，还可能损害治疗关系。"},{"en":"This preserves needed care while making attendance realistically possible.","zh":"该做法既保留必要护理，又使患者实际能够出席。"},{"en":"Immediate discharge is disproportionate when a modifiable barrier can be addressed.","zh":"当可调整的障碍可以解决时，立即终止护理并不相称。"},{"en":"Punitive scheduling prioritizes control over access and health outcomes.","zh":"惩罚性排班把控制置于可及性和健康结果之上。"}]},{"id":"poc-053","concept":"Quality Improvement","stem":"A chart audit finds that periodontal risk status is often missing. What is the BEST quality-improvement intervention?","choices":["Tell staff to remember better","Define the required field, identify workflow causes, test a prompt or checklist, and re-audit completion rates","Add risk status only to future difficult cases","Backfill records without indicating late entries"],"answer":1,"why":"Quality improvement uses a defined measure, analyzes the process, tests a change, and measures the result.","zh":"质量改进应明确指标、分析流程、测试改变并衡量结果。","pearl":"A reliable system beats a reminder floating in the air.","rationales":[{"en":"A general reminder does not identify causes or create a measurable system change.","zh":"笼统提醒既不能识别原因，也不能形成可测量的系统改变。"},{"en":"This follows a complete improvement cycle and produces measurable feedback.","zh":"该做法遵循完整改进循环并产生可测量反馈。"},{"en":"Risk status should be documented consistently, not only in selected cases.","zh":"风险状态应一致记录，而不是只用于部分病例。"},{"en":"Undisclosed late entries compromise record integrity.","zh":"未标明的事后补录会损害病历完整性。"}]},{"id":"poc-054","concept":"Referral and Collaboration","stem":"A client’s blood pressure remains severely elevated after repeat measurement, although the client reports no symptoms. What is the BEST response?","choices":["Proceed because the client feels well","Follow the clinic’s urgent medical-referral protocol, defer elective care, and document findings and communication","Diagnose hypertension and prescribe medication","Ask the client to sign consent for treatment"],"answer":1,"why":"A persistently severe reading may represent significant risk even without symptoms. The hygienist should follow established referral protocols and defer elective treatment.","zh":"即使无症状，持续严重升高的血压也可能代表重大风险。牙科卫生师应遵循既定转诊流程并推迟选择性治疗。","pearl":"Absence of symptoms does not neutralize a dangerous objective finding.","rationales":[{"en":"Feeling well does not make a persistently severe measurement safe for elective care.","zh":"感觉良好并不能使持续严重升高的读数适合选择性治疗。"},{"en":"This response appropriately manages risk, referral, deferral, and documentation.","zh":"该做法恰当处理风险、转诊、推迟治疗和记录。"},{"en":"Diagnosis and prescribing are outside the dental hygienist’s role.","zh":"诊断和开药超出牙科卫生师职责。"},{"en":"Consent cannot make an unsafe elective procedure appropriate.","zh":"知情同意不能使不安全的选择性治疗变得合适。"}]},{"id":"poc-055","concept":"Comprehensive Case","stem":"At the end of a care episode, which action BEST completes the process of care?","choices":["Close the chart after instrumentation","Compare outcomes with baseline and goals, communicate results, determine continuing needs, document, and establish an individualized maintenance or referral plan","Use the same recall interval for every client","Evaluate only whether the client liked the appointment"],"answer":1,"why":"Completion requires outcome evaluation, communication, documentation, and planning for continuing care. The cycle may begin again as needs change.","zh":"完成护理需要评价结果、沟通、记录并计划持续护理。随着需要变化，护理循环可能重新开始。","pearl":"The process ends by measuring, learning, and planning what comes next.","rationales":[{"en":"Instrumentation is implementation, not the final evaluation and continuing-care decision.","zh":"器械治疗属于实施阶段，不是最终评价和持续护理决策。"},{"en":"This choice completes evaluation and connects results to maintenance, referral, or revised care.","zh":"该选项完成评价，并把结果与维护、转诊或调整护理相连接。"},{"en":"Uniform recall ignores individual risk and response to therapy.","zh":"统一复诊间隔忽略个体风险和治疗反应。"},{"en":"Satisfaction is one outcome, but clinical and behavioural results must also be evaluated.","zh":"满意度只是一个结果，还必须评价临床和行为结果。"}]}];